Use the index sets and uniform spacings of [[def-uniform-grid-and-difference-operators]]: $x_j=jh$, $j\in\mathbb Z$, or $j$ reduced modulo $N$ in the periodic case. Fix $a>0$, $h,k>0$, and $
u=ak/h$. The target equation is the one-dimensional constant-velocity transport equation $u_t+a u_x=0$, the constant-coefficient case of [[def-linear-transport-equation-and-its-characteristic-flow]]. Set $U_j^0=u_0(jh)$ and define, for $n\ge0$,
$$  egin{aligned} 	ext{upwind: }&U_j^{n+1}=U_j^n-
u(U_j^n-U_{j-1}^n),\ 	ext{downwind: }&U_j^{n+1}=U_j^n-
u(U_{j+1}^n-U_j^n),\ 	ext{centered: }&U_j^{n+1}=U_j^n- rac{
u}{2}(U_{j+1}^n-U_{j-1}^n),\ 	ext{Lax--Friedrichs: }&U_j^{n+1}= rac{U_{j-1}^n+U_{j+1}^n}{2}- rac{
u}{2}(U_{j+1}^n-U_{j-1}^n),\ 	ext{Lax--Wendroff: }&U_j^{n+1}=U_j^n- rac{
u}{2}(U_{j+1}^n-U_{j-1}^n)+ rac{
u^2}{2}(U_{j+1}^n-2U_j^n+U_{j-1}^n). \end{aligned} $$
On a periodic grid, every index in these formulas is reduced modulo $N$; no physical boundary data are present. For $a<0$, reflect the stencil by $j\mapsto-j$ and replace $
u$ by $|a|k/h$.
